<p><a title="Link to Art Meta Major" href="https://www.ltcc.edu/academics/metamajors/meta_arts.php"><img style="float: right;" src="https://www.ltcc.edu/_resources/images/ltcc_images/academics/metamajor_icons/arts-languages-humanities-white-back.jpg" alt="Art Meta Major Icon" width="243" height="258" /></a></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>The Art degree program at Lake Tahoe Community College is designed to provide a balanced foundation in both studio art and art history. Its curriculum is focused to meet the needs of art students who are initially developing skill and concepts as well as those experienced students who seek further development. The Art Department is committed to a structured environment in which faculty and students work closely together in an atmosphere which is responsive, supportive, and facilitates experimentation.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
